`ds.lua` composition exception removal implementation plan

Approval status: approved on 2026-08-01.

This plan is authorized for implementation. It removes the temporary root
`ds.lua` dependency on `host/` without changing the public `ds` API or
replacing the established fresh source-versus-installed loading model.

Constraints:
    - Keep the public `ds` API, enums, errors, cleanup ordering, and run behavior unchanged.
    - Keep the loading helpers local to `host/execution/host.lua` and root `ds.lua`.
    - Preserve fresh `loadfile()` loading from a source checkout and installed-package fallback.
    - Do not implement the separate unified-internal-loading proposal as part of this plan.
    - Do not add a shared module loader, module-cache invalidation system, package searcher changes, or import interception.
    - Do not add file-existence-only tests, packaged-source/archive verification, or a separate source-boundary script.
    - Keep the retained host service registry, scheduler instance, cleanup registry, and project environment host-owned.

Current host-module inventory:
    - `dwarfspec.host.diagnostics.diagnostics` provides subject inspection, bounded tree and screen capture, and mount-failure formatting.
    - `dwarfspec.host.game.overlay_registration` provides project-source resolution, DFHack overlay registration staging, and exact cleanup restoration.
    - `dwarfspec.host.game.save_game_mount` provides argument validation and same-save versus transition preflight.
    - `dwarfspec.host.game.save_game_load` provides the deterministic title-screen load workflow.
    - `dwarfspec.host.game.save_game_unload` provides the deterministic no-save unload workflow.

Phase 0 - Lock the behavioral baseline:
    ☑ Run the existing unit suite and record only its command and result in the implementation handoff.
    ☑ Run the existing focused live save-game, overlay-registration, diagnostics, scheduler, and cleanup coverage.
    ☑ Confirm the current full live result and cleanup state before changing ownership.

