Phase 1 - Introduce explicit host capability interfaces:
    ☐ Define one internal run-capabilities table passed by host execution into `dwarfspec.ds.new()`.
    ☐ Provide bounded `wait_until()` and `wait_frames()` scheduling functions without exposing the scheduler implementation.
    ☐ Provide cleanup mark, labeled registration, and rollback-to-mark functions without exposing the cleanup registry.
    ☐ Provide validated project Lua-source resolution without exposing the project-environment module.
    ☐ Provide overlay file, rescan, registration-query, and path operations without exposing the retained service registry.
    ☐ Provide the immutable run identifier required for owned integration artifact names.
    ☐ Add unit coverage for capability construction, validation, and forwarding while leaving all five host imports in `ds.lua` temporarily.
    ☐ Run the unit suite.

Phase 2 - Move save-game behavior to driver ownership:
    ☐ Move save-game argument/preflight behavior to a driver-owned module and move its behavioral spec with it.
    ☐ Move the load and unload workflows to driver-owned modules and move their behavioral specs with them.
    ☐ Update the existing driver save-game commands to construct the workflows from injected scheduling and native-game capabilities.
    ☐ Remove the three `dwarfspec.host.game.save_game_*` imports from `ds.lua` after their replacement tests pass.
    ☐ Run the save-game unit specs, then the complete unit suite.
    ☐ Run focused same-save and transition live coverage and confirm cleanup.

Phase 3 - Move interaction diagnostics to driver ownership:
    ☐ Move subject inspection, bounded capture, and mount-failure formatting to a driver-owned diagnostics module with its behavioral spec.
    ☐ Inject native screen reads and window geometry so the driver module does not acquire a host dependency.
    ☐ Update driver commands and `ds.lua` composition to use the driver-owned diagnostics module.
    ☐ Remove the `dwarfspec.host.diagnostics.diagnostics` import from `ds.lua` after its replacement tests pass.
    ☐ Run the diagnostics and mount-command unit specs, then the complete unit suite.
    ☐ Run focused failure-diagnostics and recovery coverage and confirm cleanup.

Phase 4 - Split overlay registration by ownership:
    ☐ Move the run-scoped stage, rollback, and cleanup workflow to a driver-owned module with its behavioral spec.
    ☐ Keep project path resolution and external DFHack overlay/file operations behind the host-injected capabilities from Phase 1.
    ☐ Update `ds.stage_overlay_registration()` to delegate without changing its arguments, result, failure text, or cleanup guarantees.
    ☐ Remove the `dwarfspec.host.game.overlay_registration` import from `ds.lua` after its replacement tests pass.
    ☐ Run the overlay-registration unit specs, then the complete unit suite.
    ☐ Run focused overlay registration, restoration, failure-recovery, and cleanup coverage.

Phase 5 - Remove and enforce the exception:
    ☐ Add one Busted dependency-rule spec that inspects declared static imports beneath `driver/` and rejects `dwarfspec.host` targets without replacing or intercepting Lua loading.
    ☐ Confirm root `ds.lua` loads no module beneath `host/` and retains its local fresh-loading helper.
    ☐ Review that host execution still uses its unchanged local helper to fresh-load root `dwarfspec.ds` from source with installed-package fallback; do not add packaged-source or file-existence verification.
    ☐ Remove superseded host files and specs only after all behavior has moved and all references are gone.
    ☐ Update the source-organization proposal and decomposition contract to remove the temporary composition exception.
    ☐ Run syntax, formatting, declaration, and complete unit validation.

Phase 6 - Final runtime verification:
    ☐ Run the focused save-game, overlay-registration, diagnostics, scheduler, failure-recovery, and cleanup live sets.
    ☐ Run the complete live suite and compare its results and cleanup state with Phase 0.
    ☐ Confirm the service is idle with no queued or quarantined work after validation.
    ☐ Report implemented ownership changes, verification results, and any baseline-matching known failure without creating a separate evidence document.
